  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Different retention rules, one principle",
      "items": [
        "Receipts preventing duplicates expire after 7 days; administration, usage and timer-action journals after 30 days.",
        "Voice activity and observed member/channel names follow a 60-day window. Reports enforce it when read; maintenance deletes old rows and clips periods crossing the cutoff.",
        "Expired or struck timers are cleaned after the delay selected for the board, unless that cleanup is disabled. Empty inactive boards expire separately.",
        "Temporary-voice drafts expire; old records for deleted or failed channels are cleaned, along with obsolete presence records.",
        "Some completed or obsolete war-log notification records are also cleaned. Delays and triggers depend on the family; no single duration applies to the whole database.",
        "Targeted cleanup leaves other information in place. Settings and preferences do not disappear simply because a log entry or voice period has aged."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Opt-out and erasure are separate choices",
      "items": [
        "Opting out stops future observations and closes current presence. It does not delete existing history.",
        "Erasure removes the member’s events, voice periods, current presence and name. Their Discord ID, tracking choice and a protection date remain to prevent old facts from returning.",
        "Private summaries become immediately unavailable when erasure invalidates them; their physical copies are cleaned during rebuilding.",
        "Future collection depends on the member’s tracking choice: erasure alone is not a permanent opt-out."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Bot removal and requested deletion have different return rules",
      "items": [
        "Ordinary removal makes the server inactive. Returning the bot before purge reactivates the data that remains.",
        "Deletion confirmed in settings schedules purge and makes the bot leave. Returning it is insufficient: after inviting it back, an administrator must explicitly cancel deletion.",
        "The server purge delay defaults to 30 days and depends on instance configuration. Repeated events do not postpone the original deadline.",
        "Usual retention continues during the waiting period: returning before purge does not restore data that has already expired."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Scope of the erasure shown here",
      "items": [
        "Purge removes server-scoped database rows, including settings, preferences, feature data and journals.",
        "Private summaries are invalidated and then rebuilt; the diagram does not promise immediate physical deletion of all their copies.",
        "The diagram describes database records. Backups, downloaded files and content stored only in Discord are outside its scope.",
        "Automatic jobs execute cleanup and retry failures. An outage may delay physical erasure."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
